  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v0.3.0 — Sink callback and JSON formatter.\n\nAdded:\n  * LoggerOptions.ConfigureLogger — Action<LoggerConfiguration> callback for attaching extra sinks (Seq, Elastic, Application Insights, Loki) and enrichers. Invoked after built-in console/file sinks are wired, before CreateLogger().\n  * LoggerOptions.UseJsonFormatter — when true, built-in sinks emit one CompactJsonFormatter line per event (ready for log aggregators). OutputTemplate is ignored in this mode.\n  * New dependency: Serilog.Formatting.Compact 3.0.0.\n\nFixed:\n  * README API section referenced removed Flush()/FlushAsync() methods — now correctly documents Logger.Shutdown()/ShutdownAsync().\n\nv0.2.1 — Configurable file size limit.\n\nAdded:\n  * LoggerOptions.FileSizeLimitBytes (default 1 GB, null = unlimited).\n  * LoggerOptions.RollOnFileSizeLimit (default false) — roll into a new file when the size limit is hit.\n\nFixed:\n  * README configuration table now lists all LoggerOptions properties and the corrected MinimumLevel default.\n\nv0.2.0 — Major refactor.\n\nAdded:\n  * Microsoft.Extensions.Logging integration — ILogger<T> resolves from DI and writes through Serilog.\n  * AddLogger(IConfiguration, ...) overload for appsettings.json binding.\n  * Console sink (on by default) and configurable RetainedFileCountLimit (default 31).\n  * Single rolling-file mode is the new default; per-level files are opt-in via SeparateFilesPerLevel.\n  * Global AssemblyVersion enricher (cached, attached to every event).\n  * xUnit test project covering options, DI, and end-to-end writes.\n\nChanged:\n  * No longer mutates global Serilog.Log.Logger — the built ILogger is registered as a DI singleton.\n  * Logger is sealed; ILoggerConfig.Build(options) replaces Configure() (legacy method kept and marked obsolete).\n  * Invariant-culture filenames; output template uses [{Level:u3}].\n  * Stable dependencies pinned: Serilog 4.2.0, Serilog.Sinks.File 6.0.0, Serilog.Sinks.Console 6.0.0, Serilog.Extensions.Logging 9.0.0.\n  * Default MinimumLevel: Verbose -> Information.\n\nBreaking:\n  * Logger.Flush()/FlushAsync() (instance) -> Logger.Shutdown()/ShutdownAsync() (static).\n  * Two-arg Logger constructor removed; only Logger(Serilog.ILogger) remains.\n  * Default file layout is now a single rolling log.txt; set SeparateFilesPerLevel = true to restore the old layout.\n\nFull changelog: https://github.com/IoannTerrible/Serilog.TechTeaStudio.Wrap/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md",
